============================================================================
WHAT EACH TOOL SEES AS 'THE HOT THING'  (oracle: gemm owns 69% of GPU time)
============================================================================
  wall_nosync : a single iteration = 37.0 us  (7x under-report)
  cProfile    : run_loop (CPU-side launch, 37099 us over 150 iters) - says nothing about the GPU
  py-spy      : gemm owns 10% of CPU samples (launch side; GPU invisible)
  torch.profiler: void cutlass::Kernel2<cutlass_80_simt_sgemm_ (164.8 us/iter) - right kernel, right time
  nsys        : void cutlass::Kernel2<cutlass_80_simt_sgemm_ (166.0 us/iter averaged over the recording)
  device mem  : 151 MiB on the device, invisible to host RSS tools

